the energy union is at the top of the  agenda of the next tte council EU  ministers will exchange views on a  strategic framework proposed by the  commission the aim is giving consumers  secure sustainable competitive and  affordable energy while addressing the  existing challenges in the sector it  also seeks to contribute to attaining  the 20 30 goals on climate and energy in  June 2014 the european council  established a strategic agenda for the  union in times of change with energy and  climate policies being one of its five  building blocks the outcome of the  debate will be forwarded to the  President of the European Council ahead  of the March meeting of EU leaders  ministers will also hold a policy debate  on the developments and priorities for  energy infrastructure the debate will  focus on key measures to further promote  the implementation of an interconnected  cross-border energy market including  ending the energy isolation of member  states ways of improving investment for  the energy sector will also be discussed  as well as regional cooperation in order  to achieve the ten percent minimum  target of electricity interconnections  by 2020 the outcome of the debate will  figure in the Presidency's report on  Europe 2020 strategy
 

